    "quote": "authentic, not staged?",
    "context_summary": "Carmen reviews ad copy for Love Like Wild photographer Shannon Lee. Initial drafts say 'No posing, just real moments' and 'No awkward posing.' Shannon pushes back that she does pose people (just not awkwardly), taking roughly 90% candids. They settle on 'authentic, not staged' because she doesn't stage or fake moments during the day.",
    "moment_type": "decision",
    "proposition": "A single word in ad copy can misrepresent your service and repel your ideal client.",
    "audience_relevance": "Photographers and other visual vendors often market a style that isn't absolute; small wording choices shape who applies and who books.",
    "qualifications": [
      "Client-specific ad copy review, not a measured A/B test.",
      "The final wording was a judgment call between vendor and agency, not validated against performance."
    ],
    "claim_status": "reported",
    "sensitivity": "public_candidate",
    "strength": 4.0,
    "reasons": [
      "Reveals a concrete positioning correction that changes who the ad attracts.",
      "Shows the vendor's own clarification of what she does versus what the copy implied."
    ]
  },
