    "quote": "20% of people go from the page",
    "context_summary": "Carmen and Fallon review a destination-wedding-planner client whose Meta ads are clear but whose landing page is vague above the fold. About 20% of visitors reach the inquiry form but don't submit. Fallon notes Meta visitors arrive with ad context; Google visitors don't, so the page must carry the explanation.",
    "moment_type": "result",
    "proposition": "When ads promise clarity, the landing page must deliver it or traffic leaks at the form.",
    "audience_relevance": "Any vendor running paid search must make sure the page answers 'what do you actually do?' before asking for contact info.",
    "qualifications": [
      "One client's observed behavior, not a controlled test.",
      "The 20% figure is an internal estimate, not audited."
    ],
    "claim_status": "reported",
    "sensitivity": "internal_only",
    "strength": 4.0,
    "reasons": [
      "Connects a specific leak (reach form, no submit) to a specific cause (vague hero section).",
      "Distinguishes Meta from Google traffic, which changes what the page must prove."
    ]
  },
